        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0201" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg101"/>

                <head>No. 48.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Young
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 8, 1884.</date>
                        (Received September 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 494.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose you a copy of
                    the recent convention between China and France. The Department will note, in
                    parallel columns, a translation into English from both the French and Chinese
                    texts. While the French text must be accepted as conveying the exact meaning of
                    the treaty, the variation in forms of expression and the evident intent of the
                    writers is worthy of attention.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN RUSSELL YOUNG.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d48-a1.xml" xpointer="d48-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
